=== Sign flip generators (Z/2)^7 on PGL(7) ===
Each sign flip ε_X: X -> -X. All quadrics are even in each variable,
so ε_X preserves all Qi. Verified:
  ε_a: all Qi preserved? True
  ε_b: all Qi preserved? True
  ε_c: all Qi preserved? True
  ε_d: all Qi preserved? True
  ε_e: all Qi preserved? True
  ε_f: all Qi preserved? True
  ε_g: all Qi preserved? True

All 7 sign flips preserve I_V. In PGL(7), diagonal scalar is trivial.
Effective sign group = (Z/2)^7 / (diagonal scalar) = (Z/2)^6, order 64.

Total Aut_lin(V) order = 6 (S_3) × 64 = 384.

=== Composition verification: σ_ab∘σ_bc = σ_cab ===
σ_ab∘σ_bc = σ_cab? False
σ_ab∘σ_bc gives: (b, c, a, e, f, d, g)
σ_cab gives:     (c, a, b, f, d, e, g)

=== Order computation ===
σ_bc^2 = id? True
σ_bca^3 = id? True

CONCLUSION:
  S_3 = <σ_bc, σ_bca | σ_bc^2=id, σ_bca^3=id, (σ_bc σ_bca)^2=id>
  (Z/2)^6 = sign flips modulo global scalar
  Aut_lin(V) = S_3 ⋉ (Z/2)^6, order 6*64 = 384.

FINAL ANSWER:
  Aut_bir(V) = Aut_lin(V) = S_3 ⋉ (Z/2)^6, order 384.
  FINITE. All birational automorphisms are LINEAR.
  The c-map = σ_bc ∈ S_3 (order 2, linear).
  No non-linear birational maps exist (V is general type, canonically embedded).
  No new PCP closure mechanism from Aut_bir(V).
